\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab He wants not friends that hath Thy love,
\par \pard\li720 And may converse and walk with Thee,
\par And with Thy saints here and above
\par With whom for ever I must be.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab In the communion of the saints
\par \pard\li720 Is wisdom, safety and delight ;
\par And, when my heart declines and faints,
\par It's raised by their heat and light !
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab As for my friends, they are not lost ;
\par \pard\li720 The several vessels of Thy fleet,
\par Though parted now, by tempests tost,
\par Shall safely in the haven meet.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\tab Still we are centred all in Thee,
\par \pard\li720 Members, though distant, of one Head ;
\par In the same family we be,
\par By the same faith and spirit and led.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Before Thy throne we daily meet,
\par As joint petitioners to Thee ;
\par In spirit we each other greet,
\par And shall again each other see.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  The heavenly hosts, world without end,
\par Shall be my company above ;
\par And Thou, my best and surest Friend,
\par Who shall divide me from Thy love ?
\par \pard 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

